This is the final, production-ready solution that addresses the Regex Parsing Issue (nested brackets) and aligns the Padding/Sign logic with your reference output (0L01A0000000086726535.030).
1. The Database Solution (SQL)
The core problem was that your Regex contains brackets (e.g., [0-9]). When we put that inside configuration brackets [regex], the parser gets confused.
The Fix: We will wrap the Regex in DOUBLE QUOTES inside the brackets in the database (e.g., ["^[ALS]..."]). The Java code will then look specifically for these quotes.
